=== Adultery under the Law
--- The Adulterer and the Adulteress Shall Surely Be Put to Death
kicker: Leviticus 20:10 · A Capital Offense, Both Parties
scripture: Leviticus 20:10 | mark: the adulterer and the adulteress shall surely be put to death

--- So Shalt Thou Put Away Evil from Israel
kicker: Deuteronomy 22:22–24 · Stoning, Both the Man and the Woman
scripture: Deuteronomy 22:22-24 | mark: Then ye shall bring them both out unto the gate of that city, and ye shall stone them with stones that they die

--- The Woman Taken in Adultery [title]
overline: John 8:1–11
heading: The Woman Taken in Adultery

--- Moses in the law commanded
scripture: John 8:1-6 | mark: Now Moses in the law commanded us, that such should be stoned: but what sayest thou?

--- He that is without sin
scripture: John 8:7-11 | mark: He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone at her.; And Jesus said unto her, Neither do I condemn thee: go, and sin no more.
callout: The Law demanded death for both parties, yet only the woman was brought. Jesus did not abolish the Law; He exposed the accusers’ own guilt. His verdict was not cheap grace, “go, and sin no more,” but mercy that upheld the standard while extending redemption. Grace does not erase the Law; it fulfills it.

