kicker: Revelation 19:7–9 · The Marriage of the Lamb Is Come
scripture: Revelation 19:7-9 | mark: Let us be glad and rejoice, and give honour to him: for the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made herself ready; fine linen, clean and white; righteousness of saints

--- A Great Multitude in White Robes
kicker: Revelation 7:9, 13–14 · The Invited, Robes of White
scripture: Revelation 7:9; Revelation 7:13-14 | mark: a great multitude, which no man could number

--- King of Kings, and Lord of Lords
kicker: Revelation 19:11–16 · The Bridegroom, Christ the King
scripture: Revelation 19:11-16 | mark: Faithful and True; The Word of God; clothed in fine linen, white and clean

--- Prepared as a Bride Adorned for Her Husband
kicker: Revelation 21:2, 9–11 · New Jerusalem, the Bride Adorned
scripture: Revelation 21:2; Revelation 21:9-11 | mark: And I John saw the holy city, new Jerusalem, coming down from God out of heaven, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.; the bride, the Lamb’s wife

=== Marriage: From Eden to Eternity
--- Marriage: From Eden to Eternity
kicker: The Full Picture · Genesis to Revelation
p: The Bible opens with a wedding: one man, one woman, one flesh in the garden of God. The Bible closes with a wedding: the Lamb and His bride, the redeemed of all ages, clothed in white, gathered at the marriage supper of the Lamb.
p: Every earthly marriage is a shadow of that eternal union. Christ is the Bridegroom. The Church is His bride. He gave Himself for her, He is coming for her, and He will present her to Himself: holy, without blemish, in fine linen, clean and white.
big: Ephesians 5:32
note: What therefore God hath joined together, let not man put asunder. [[Matthew 19:6]]
